(   Layer  |  Implementation ) Tj
T*
(  ------- | ----------------) Tj
T*
(   Message & key-wrap crypto  |  Client app \(Flutter / Dart\) via open-source libraries) Tj
T*
(`encrypt` and `pointycastle` ) Tj
T*
(   Private key storage  |  iOS Keychain via `flutter_secure_storage` ) Tj
T*
(   Network transport  |  Apple OS TLS / HTTPS to Supabase and Firebase ) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Cryptography for chat is implemented **in the application**, in addition to encryption) Tj
T*
(provided by the Apple operating system \(HTTPS\). It is **not** limited to Apple OS APIs such as) Tj
T*
(CryptoKit for message payloads.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Source of truth in the codebase: `lib/services/encryption_service.dart`.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(---) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4. What is encrypted) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(? **Encrypted:** chat message body ciphertext; per-conversation AES keys wrapped under each) Tj
T*
(participant?s RSA public key) Tj
T*
(? **Not encrypted by custom app crypto:** public profile fields intended for discovery; push) Tj
T*
(notification bodies \(generic text only\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Key lifecycle \(summary\):) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Each device generates an RSA-2048 identity key pair; public wrap key is stored on the user) Tj
T*
(profile.) Tj
T*
(2. When a conversation starts, a random 256-bit conversation key is generated.) Tj
T*
(3. That key is RSA-OAEP wrapped for each participant and stored server-side as opaque) Tj
T*
(ciphertext.) Tj
T*
(4. Messages are AES-256-CBC encrypted with the conversation key; ciphertext is) Tj
T*
(stored/transmitted as Base64\(IV ? ciphertext\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(---) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
